    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and verified. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Problem\nThe `frai gate init --ci` command via the CLI was not passing the `--ci` flag through to the underlying `frai-gate` process, so the GitHub Actions workflow file (`.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`) was never being created, even though the FRAI-SPEC.md file was.\n\n## Root Cause\nWhen using Commander.js with global options and a subcommand with rest parameters (`[args...]`), global options are consumed by the main program before being passed to the subcommand. The `gate` command's action handler was only receiving the positional arguments (`['init']`) without the flag (`--ci`).\n\n## Solution\nModified the `gate` command's action handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to:\n1. Accept the Commander.js `commandObj` as a third parameter\n2. Access the parent command's parsed options via `commandObj.parent?.opts?.()`\n3. Explicitly reconstruct the argument list to include the `--ci` flag before spawning the `frai-gate` process\n\n## Verification\n\u2705 Tested `frai gate init --ci` which now correctly:\n- Creates `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n- Creates `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` with the proper GitHub Actions workflow content\n\nThe package has been rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build` and is ready to use.",
